descriptions.job-15ss1t6:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Product&amp;nbsp; - Connect Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect is Stripe’s platform for businesses that serve other businesses. It gives platforms the infrastructure to represent the people and companies in their ecosystem, onboard and verify them, manage their accounts, accept payments, and pay them out - without building payments, compliance, or financial-services systems themselves. This is how businesses like Shopify can help entrepreneurs run and grow their businesses. It is also the kind of infrastructure that marketplaces such as DoorDash need to coordinate money movement across large networks of restaurants, merchants, and dashers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect has impact across industries. &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/shopify&quot;&gt;Shopify&lt;/a&gt; uses Stripe to embed financial services for merchants; &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/lugg&quot;&gt;Lugg&lt;/a&gt; streamlines worker onboarding and offers instant payouts; &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/doorloop&quot;&gt;DoorLoop&lt;/a&gt; reduces manual customer onboarding tasks by nearly 50% with Stripe; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/sharetribe&quot;&gt;Sharetribe&lt;/a&gt; helps entrepreneurs launch and run marketplaces on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is accelerating the emergence of entirely new business models: global networks of creators and experts, AI-native marketplaces, and agent-driven products that change how people discover, buy, sell, and deliver services. These businesses are more dynamic than traditional platforms: participants may operate across borders, take on different roles, and need new ways to establish trust, access financial capabilities, and get paid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Connect Abstractions team owns the platform primitives that make these models possible. We are building the foundational abstractions for representing participants, onboarding them safely, configuring their capabilities, and managing their lifecycle on Stripe. Our work will determine how quickly the next generation of platforms can launch, how flexibly they can evolve, and how much of Stripe they can bring to the businesses and people they serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a chance to define a foundational product area at Stripe. You will turn a fast-changing set of user and product needs into durable platform primitives that work across products, industries, and geographies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines high-leverage strategy with hands-on product execution. You will work through ambiguous, consequential questions like: what should a platform be able to model? What should be simple by default but flexible when needed? How can Stripe make complex financial infrastructure feel effortless for a platform and its users?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The outcome of your work will compound. The abstractions you help create will be reused across Connect and Stripe, shaping what new products platforms can build and how quickly they can bring them to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an entrepreneurial Product Manager to build the platform experiences behind Connect&#39;s next generation of users. You will own critical product primitives that platforms, including the fastest-growing AI companies, use to onboard, configure, and manage their users on Stripe. You will turn a clear strategic direction into products that solve hard user problems today while creating a coherent, extensible foundation for business models that are still being invented.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for someone who enjoys the depth of platform work but is uncompromising about product craft and solving real user needs - both the ones users have today and will have in the future. The work is not building infra for its own sake; you will build capabilities that help our users launch a new marketplace, enable a global network to pay its contributors, or give a business entirely new ways for their end users to earn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the next generation of Connect accounts to life. Own key product areas within the account platform, translating strategy into a focused roadmap, crisp product decisions, and high-quality launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build from use cases. Start with the real problems platforms face, such as onboarding a new seller, supporting a complex business model, or evolving a user&#39;s financial capabilities, and then work towards the primitives needed to solve them well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sophisticated infrastructure feel simple. Partner with engineering and design to create API and product experiences that are powerful and intuitive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See around corners. Develop a strong point of view on how AI will change platform economics, participant models, and financial workflows. Make focused foundational investments that unlock the next wave of demand.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn user signals into durable product investments. Work closely with users, Sales, Partnerships, and other Stripe teams to distinguish bespoke requests from patterns that should become scalable platform capabilities, connecting business needs, user needs, and platform evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high-velocity, high-craft execution and own outcomes. Lead cross-functional work from discovery through launch, and hold yourself accountable for developer experience, platform adoption, user value, and business impact, not simply features shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a product builder who can move easily between a user’s hardest problem, the business opportunity behind it, and the product decisions needed to solve it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have worked on technically complex products - such as APIs, developer tools, shared platform capabilities, or core product experiences - but you do not build tech/platform for its own sake. You see strong platform design as a way to help users move faster, create better products, and unlock new business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are opinionated, thoughtful, and execution-oriented. You can focus a team on the few decisions that matter most, create momentum in ambiguous situations, and ship products that raise the bar for both quality and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience, with meaningful time owning platform, API, or developer-facing products end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own a product area end to end: setting strategy, driving execution, and measuring outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical instincts and comfort defining the measurement framework before you ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication and the ability to build alignment across functions and levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience productizing bespoke or custom solutions into broadly available platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of making well-judged foundational investments ahead of user demand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-0pe87e2:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Ondo Finance. Our mission is to provide institutional-grade, blockchain-enabled investment products and services. We have both a technology arm that develops decentralized finance technology, and an asset management arm that creates and manages tokenized funds. We are the global leader in tokenized treasuries, tokenized stocks and ETFs, and are building the future of institutional-grade financial services onchain.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Founded by folks from Goldman Sachs Digital Assets Team, we’re backed by some of the best investors in the world including Founders Fund, Coinbase Ventures, Pantera Capital, Tiger Global, and more. We are currently the leaders in the space in terms of AUM and are well capitalized to continue growing the firm. We&#39;re fully remote, with team members across the U.S.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;You&#39;ll design the products at the core of&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://app.ondo.finance&quot;&gt;app.ondo.finance&lt;/a&gt; — where private clients, high-value investors, and primary-market participants access, subscribe to, and manage sophisticated financial instruments across blockchain ecosystems. This role blends strategic thinking with hands-on execution: you&#39;ll shape product direction while shipping polished, end-to-end experiences in close collaboration with Product, Engineering, and Research.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring across mid and senior levels, and the scope of ownership will be calibrated to your experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex financial concepts and user needs into intuitive, trustworthy product experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design end-to-end flows, wireframes, prototypes, and high-fidelity UI for web and mobile&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to (and at senior level, drive) product strategy alongside Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build on and evolve our design system, including documentation and tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering through implementation to ensure quality and accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define design success metrics and measure the impact of your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;3+ years of product design experience designing web or mobile products, with experience shipping fintech, trading, investing, or banking products strongly preferred.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You Love Design Craft&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Craft&lt;/strong&gt;. High-bar UI and interaction design; your portfolio shows end-to-end systems and polish, not single screens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complexity translation.&lt;/strong&gt; You make dense, regulated, high-stakes financial information feel simple and trustworthy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems thinking.&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to design scalable, cohesive experiences by considering how individual features fit into the broader product ecosystem and design system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a Collaborator&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; influence.&lt;/strong&gt; You enjoy building strong cross-functional partnerships and are able to effectively influences decisions across Product, Engineering, and other project stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-direction and communication.&lt;/strong&gt; You thrive in a remote, low-oversight environment and can communicate your design thinking clearly to Product, Engineering, and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You Think in Products&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product thinking.&lt;/strong&gt; You frame the problem before the solution, connect design decisions to business outcomes, and can push back on scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-end ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; You take work from discovery through flows, high-fidelity design, engineering handoff, and shipping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You Lead with Curiousity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous learning.&lt;/strong&gt; You love to learn new domains and seek to understand complex concepts. You treat mistakes as chances to learn; quick to be wrong, quick to pivot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI workflows or AI-usage in the product design process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fintech/financial product experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in crypto (DeFi, exchanges, wallets, stablecoins, tokenization/RWAs, custody, or onchain analytics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experimentation and metrics fluency (A/B testing, data-driven design)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with collaborating with user research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribution to or management of design systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation including but not limited to salary, future token rights, and/or equity (according to your preferences) — We are well-funded and believe that great talent deserves great compensation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full benefits (medical, vision, and dental) and flexible vacation policy (PTO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-first team across many countries — You will be an early team member helping shape our vision, culture, and design practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A+ colleagues — Our team includes alumni from: Goldman Sachs, Blackrock, Two Sigma, Bridgewater, SpaceX, AWS, Meta, Google, McKinsey, Circle, Uniswap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-class investors — We are proud to be backed by leading crypto experts and VCs, including Pantera Capital, Founders Fund and Coinbase Ventures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;

descriptions.job-0v0ddbe:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team &amp;amp; role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for a senior operator and systems thinker to join the Central Strategy and Operations (S&amp;amp;O) team. This is a senior individual contributor role for someone who is obsessed with how organizations actually work and who builds the infrastructure that makes Stripe faster, clearer, and more coordinated as it scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Central S&amp;amp;O sits at the center of how Stripe runs as a company. This role specifically owns the machinery of company operations—the planning processes, operating rhythms, information architecture, and cross-functional systems that let the leadership team at Stripe make better decisions, faster. If you&#39;re the kind of person who looks at a broken process and immediately starts designing the system that replaces it—and who reaches for automation before asking for headcount—this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work across the most senior leaders at Stripe and partner teams to design, run, and continuously improve the operational systems that connect strategy to execution. This is not a coordination or program management role. It&#39;s a build role. You&#39;ll own outcomes end-to-end and raise the operational ceiling of the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run planning for Stripe. You&#39;ll own and execute how Stripe does annual planning including multiple offshoot workstreams, and the frameworks leadership uses to make decisions. Continuous improvement of existing processes, automating manual workflows and helping us redesign lighter ways to do the work in the future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, automate, and scale central operations infrastructure. You&#39;ll identify where manual, repetitive, or fragmented processes are creating drag and replace them with scalable systems—whether that&#39;s working with others on structured data pipelines, AI-augmented workflows, or new tooling. Your first instinct is to build, not to coordinate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate strategy into operational reality. Help teams drive strategic discussions in leadership forums with your thinking and architecture. Prepare and run leadership-level operating forums, bring your own point of view into the room, and own the follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous operational improvement. You&#39;ll have direct working relationships with the most senior leaders at Stripe and challenge assumptions, not just execute against them. You&#39;ll maintain a running view of where the operational systems of the company are breaking down—where decisions are slow, handoffs are unclear, or accountability is diffuse—and work across teams to address root causes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of work experience, with a significant portion in operational roles at high-growth tech companies—product operations, strategy and operations, business operations, or company or corporate planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building and owning operational systems. You have measurably improved how a company or large team operates, not just managed existing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience either with company or functional planning—annual planning, OKR and SOKR-style goal-setting, resource allocation, and operating cadence design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems thinker who is automation-first—you instinctively reach for tools, data pipelines, and AI-augmented workflows to reduce manual overhead and increase leverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical rigor—you&#39;re comfortable owning data and metrics directly, running your own analyses, and pressure-testing assumptions without relying on a dedicated analytics partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with and presenting to C-suite and senior executive stakeholders. You&#39;re comfortable owning the room and bringing a sharp, independent perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High comfort with ambiguity—you take an undefined operational problem, scope it, design a solution, and drive it to completion with minimal oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency in AI tools in order to automate workflows as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying automation-thinking and scaled approaches to operational workflows—from analysis and synthesis to systems and decision support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a technology company is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in fintech, management consulting, or investment banking is a plus, but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the product and infrastructure ecosystem at Stripe or similar complex platform businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with modern planning tools, workflow automation platforms, and operational data infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-0ll8siy:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who are we?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FalconX is a pioneering team of operators, investors, and builders committed to revolutionizing institutional access to the crypto markets. Operating at the intersection of traditional finance and  cutting-edge technology, FalconX addresses the industry&#39;s foremost challenges: Navigating the digital asset market can be complex and fragmented, with limited products and services that support trading strategies, structures, and liquidity found in conventional financial markets. As a comprehensive solution for all digital asset strategies from start to scale, FalconX operates as the connective tissue empowering clients with seamless navigation through the ever- evolving cryptocurrency landscape.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Head of Risk - Malta&lt;/strong&gt; is responsible to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set up and manage the Risk Management Framework&lt;/strong&gt;: Establish appropriate risk policies and procedures to minimize the Company’s risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommend updates to the Risk Appetite Statement:&lt;/strong&gt; Advise the Board of Directors on annual updates and appropriate risk tolerance limits, clearly outlining the level of risk acceptable in line with strategic goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;a risk register&lt;/strong&gt;: Systematically record identified risks and mitigation actions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify, analyze, quantify, and mitigate risks&lt;/strong&gt;: Address risks faced by the Company with appropriate actions. The risk identification should encompass not only integrity risks (such as AML/CFT and fraud) but also ICT, operational, market, credit, legal, compliance, conflicts of interests, and other relevant risks in accordance with all intended crypto-asset services. The risk identification process should address risks at various levels, including individual business lines and the overall entity together with outsourced activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conduct ongoing risk assessments:&lt;/strong&gt; Regularly evaluate risks to ensure they are managed effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Credit and Counterparty Risk Management&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp; Design, enforce and monitor credit risk policies and oversee exposures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Implement risk measurement methodologies:&lt;/strong&gt; Recommend risk appetite thresholds and develop monitoring tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ensure compliance with regulatory requirements:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain activities within relevant risk-related regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate with senior management:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage key risks, provide analysis, and highlight risk exposures and performance metrics. Also coordinate cross-functionally with business units to refine risk controls and support new product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead regional incident response and crisis management efforts:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee responses to incidents and crises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop specific risk management actions:&lt;/strong&gt; Create targeted strategies to reduce or control risk exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitor and report on risk management activities:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement continuous monitoring systems and regular reporting to management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluate the risk management framework annually:&lt;/strong&gt; Assess its effectiveness, relevance, and adequacy in addressing emerging risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay updated on industry trends and emerging risks&lt;/strong&gt;: Adapt strategies to reflect changes in the environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;General&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the preparation of reports for the Board of Directors, senior management, auditors, and regulatory authorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to information requests from regulators and auditors, and provide assistance during thematic reviews conducted by these parties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in meetings as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Head of Risk has to undergo the MFSA PQ process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;The incumbent is expected to have,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;familiarity with the operations of the crypto, investment, or banking sectors will be considered an advantage;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;relevant qualification in financial services or compliance is required;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;strong verbal and written communication skills, sound judgment, and analytical abilities;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;follow-up skills and the ability to communicate clearly and promptly are essential;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;team player skills with a genuine interest in digital assets and blockchain technology; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;enthusiasm for continuous learning and a willingness to explore new frontiers in technology and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;message-list_1784193026.312409&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
